MView Day 22 (2026-09-30)
=========================

A photo that stayed half blocky (user)
--------------------------------------
test\images\problem\2014412163548_4.jpg (3264 x 2448, a phone photo;
private, not for the repository: test\images\* is ignored). Some parts
of the picture stayed coarse and blocky, the rest was sharp; the
diagnostics line said "sharpening 3 / 12".
- The file is fine (PIL and MView decode it completely; a few zero bytes
  after the end marker, harmless).
- Cause: the GPU renderer shows a large image first from its small screen
  copy, then uploads the full image tile by tile (12 tiles of 1022 px
  here), one step per frame, and asked for the next frame with
  FControl.Invalidate at the end of Paint. TOpenGLControl.Invalidate
  does nothing while the control paints (csCustomPaint, LCL
  openglcontext.pas), so the next step only came when something else
  repainted the view (mouse, info line, timer events). Here nothing did
  after 3 tiles: 9 tiles stayed at the screen copy's resolution.
- Fix: uGLRenderer marks the window itself (LCLIntf.InvalidateRect on its
  handle), which is kept during the paint; and TMView.PumpDeliveries
  repaints every 50 ms while the renderer reports IsUploading (safety
  net).
Units changed: uGLRenderer, uMView.

Leaving the tree upwards (user)
-------------------------------
"i want an ini 'parse 1 level upwards' (1/0) entry that allows leaving
the accessible directory tree - by one level upwards ... if i start by
passing an image to mview that is in a dir that has no own sub
directories, i can now travel successively upwards and explore the
tree." / "it does not work ... on dirs stored in the side panel. i am
locked in the set directory".
- Opening a folder (the side panel, a drop) makes that folder the root;
  with WrapScope=Dir (the user's setting) the image steps stay in the
  folder, and the folder steps (gestures left / right, tilt) had nowhere
  to go: locked in.
- New [Navigation] ClimbUp=1 (default 0): a step that runs past the end
  of the tree doesn't wrap; TNavigator reports ClimbWanted, TMView opens
  the root's parent keeping the current image, and when that tree has
  been scanned it does the same step again, which lands in the old
  root's neighbouring folder. Repeats level by level, up to one level
  below the drive or network share (CanClimbUp); there it wraps as
  before. Preloading no longer looks round to the tree's start while
  climbing is possible.
- The gesture up (ParentFolder) still widens the tree by one level at
  any time.
- Review (independent) found and fixed: fast steps at the end restarted
  the climb (and cleared the cache) again and again: steps now wait while
  the folder above is read and the last one is done then (not longer than
  20 s); the replayed step could jump from a place the user had moved
  on to (same fix); climbing and Parent folder no longer throw away the
  decoded images (OpenMedia AKeepCache); climbing needs Recursive=1.
  Noted: while a very large image goes to the GPU (1-2 s at 100 MP) the
  frames follow each other so closely that the 50 ms timer waits for the
  upload to finish (Windows gives paints priority over timers).
- TestNavigation: TestClimbUp (11 checks).
Units changed: uNavigator, uMView, uConfig. Spec §10, §14.

Zoom centre in the 4-zone mode (user)
-------------------------------------
"in single screen mode, the center of zooming is the mouse pointer. that
is great. in 4-zone mode the zoom center should be the center of the
screen, otherwise the image moves to the top left corner."
- uMouseEngine: ZoomIn / ZoomOut with the zones on zoom at the middle of
  the view (the engine's view size); zones off: at the mouse as before.
  Zoom mode (X1) keeps zooming at the mouse (the mouse can be anywhere
  there, and pointing is the point of it).
- TestMouse: the Inspect-zone check now expects the middle; zoom mode
  checked to stay at the mouse.
Units changed: uMouseEngine. Spec §9.2.

