Display filters, step 1 (Phase H "Looking closer", proposed name)
------------------------------------------------------------------
User: "big improvement!!! shall we get into the filter implementation?
is this btw still phase G, or shall we call it something else?"
Proposed: Phase H, "Looking closer" (filters and magnifier; G4 / G6 in
Strategy_Phase_G.md). Not yet confirmed by the user.
- uFilters (new): the maths, one definition for both renderers, in a
  fixed order: black / white point -> brightness / contrast -> gamma ->
  saturation / hue (YIQ, the luma stays) -> invert. Ranges, neutral
  values, wheel steps, bar positions (gamma on a log scale, 1.0 in the
  middle), the file name suffix for "apply to a copy" (step 2).
- GPU (uGLRenderer): MView's first shader, a GLSL 1.10 fragment shader
  over the existing tiles; the OpenGL 2.0 functions loaded at run time.
  A filter change costs one frame, also at 100 MP. Without shaders:
  FiltersAvailable False, the panel and the info line say so.
- CPU (uRenderer): the filters on a copy of the screen-sized part only.
- Filter panel (uFilterPanel, new) at the left edge: opens by resting
  there (the sort panel's EdgeDelayMs / EdgeWidth), menu "Filters (side
  menu, left)", command FilterPanel; pin [Filters] Pinned; a lock in the
  header. Wheel over a row = a step, left drag = relative adjust, double-
  click = reset that filter, Invert = click; Reset all; a hint line.
  The renderers got a second panel slot (SetFilterPanel).
- Lock filters: menu (ticked), the panel's lock, command LockFilters.
  Unlocked, a new file starts unfiltered; a crop keeps the filters.
- "[filtered]" / "[filtered, locked]" in the info line.
- Commands FilterPanel, LockFilters, ResetFilters (mouse profile, none
  bound by default). Esc closes the filter panel after the sort panel.
- Review (independent) found and fixed before delivery: FPC's Format
  has no "+" flag (the panel would have raised on every redraw); the
  shader lifted blacks at low gamma (an epsilon in pow); a click on a
  row could snap a small value to neutral (now only a real drag moves
  it, and the snap is smaller than a wheel step); the "not available"
  note when the shader fails at its first use; a program not deleted
  after a failed link; the filtered copy kept after a reset.
- TestFilters (new, plain fpc): 38 checks. build_test.bat runs it.
Units new: uFilters, uFilterPanel. Changed: uRenderer, uGLRenderer,
uMView, uCommands, uMouseProfile, uMouseEngine, uConfig, umainform.
Spec §9.8, §14, §15; Strategy_Phase_G.md G4.
Step 2 (next): histogram, Auto (Fiji-like, the selection as ROI), "Apply
filters to a copy".

Display filters, step 2: Auto, histogram, apply to a copy
---------------------------------------------------------
User: "it works very nicely!! what about the dynamic range? is this
planned as auto setting?" - proposed Auto as a click (once) and a
double-click (for every image); user: "yes, that is great".
- uFilters: THistogram, AutoLevels (Fiji-like, 0.35 % saturated, half
  at each end; at least 3 levels apart, else nothing changes).
- uFilterImage (new): ApplyFiltersToBitmap (moved out of uRenderer),
  ImageHistogram (luma, sampled to about 1 million pixels).
- Filter panel: a histogram under the header (image, or the edit-mode
  selection), black / white points marked; an Auto button next to Reset
  all, lit while on for every image.
- TMView: Auto once / for every image ([auto] in the info line; every
  new image and its better version get their own points; a selection
  re-levels live); a manual black / white change ends it. "Apply filters
  to a copy" (menu, command ApplyFilters): a new image like a crop, named
  after the filters; locked filters come back with the next file.
- Review (independent) found and fixed: the histogram key used the
  bitmap's address (animations re-levelled every frame; now the first
  frame and a display counter); Auto could set the points closer than
  the panel allows; locked filters lost after "apply to a copy"; Auto on
  a flat image kept the previous image's points; a just-started
  selection of a few pixels gave extreme stretches.
- TestFilters: TestAuto (4 checks), 42 checks in all.
Units new: uFilterImage. Changed: uFilters, uRenderer, uFilterPanel,
uMView, uCommands, uMouseProfile, uMouseEngine, umainform. Spec §9.8.

