Evening: user's test round
--------------------------
User tested step 1 and 2: "the permanent auto function of filter
processing is incredible!!! it could be a default setting"; "the 'one
level up' directory scan does now work, the ini entry climb up is
efficient". Changes asked for, all done:
- Filter panel: the pin at the left of the header (next to the window's
  edge), the lock right of it, then the title.
- "Mirror left / right" in the filter panel (an inverted microscope's
  images are mirrored): a toggle like Invert. Geometry in the renderers
  (GPU: negative x scale; CPU: mirrored copy before the quarter turns);
  ScreenToImage / ImageToScreen follow, so selection, crop and ROI stay
  right. Goes with Lock / Reset, [mirrored] in the info line, _mirror and
  mirrored pixels in "Apply filters to a copy".
- [Filters] AutoFilter=1 (default on): Auto for every image from the
  start.
- Info line: "52 % = 1997 x 1331" (size on screen).
- "Resize to the size shown (W x H)" (menu, command ResizeToShown):
  copy / move / save always used the original size; this makes a copy at
  the shown size (like a crop), which Save / Save as / the sort panel
  then write. Chosen instead of a size choice inside the save dialogs:
  it works for the sort panel too, the same way as crop and "apply
  filters to a copy".
- Settings screen: "Total Commander side by side" button: MView left,
  Total Commander right, in [Startup] LastDirectory, else Documents.
- Review (independent): no compile problems found; fixed: a double-click
  on a toggle row switched it twice; the "filters not available" note
  (GPU without shaders) repeated on every image with AutoFilter on (now
  once); mirrored + 180 degrees made two full copies on the CPU (now
  one); the Total Commander note says to Save the path first.
- TestFilters: TestMirror (11 checks), 53 checks in all.
Units changed: uFilters, uFilterImage, uRenderer, uGLRenderer,
uFilterPanel, uMView, uCommands, uMouseProfile, uMouseEngine, uConfig,
uIniEditor, umainform. Spec §9.7, §9.8, §14.
